## CerpacNAS validation policy

- Root login is intentional, but work only in the assigned `jw` workspace below `/root/Projects`.
- Never use `sudo`, Docker, package-manager mutation, or dangerous sandbox/approval bypass flags.
- Set `JULIA_NUM_THREADS=1`; run one lane at a time through `nas validate`, which enforces a 180-second limit and records peak RSS.
- Allowed by default: web format, pure tests, type-check, and Julia format check.
- A focused Julia lane must first pass `nas validate thesis <task> focus:<seam> --calibrate`.
- A lane that exceeds 180 seconds or 3 GiB peak RSS is disabled on this NAS.
- Never run `validate all`, `validate evidence`, the thesis evidence gate, benchmarks, browser tests, or API-live tests.
- Leave performance conclusions and final acceptance for Mac or CI; list skipped checks in the handoff report.
- Never push unless `nas handoff ... --push` explicitly authorizes the selected `wip/...` bookmark. Never move `main`.
